+
+### Vendored native build controls
+
+The fallback requires C++17, OpenMP and CMake >= 3.18. Configuration uses
+`CMAKE` when explicitly set, otherwise a sufficiently recent `cmake3` or
+`cmake`. The generated link flags use the C++ and OpenMP runtimes discovered
+by CMake, including Clang/libomp toolchains.
+
+Native compilation is capped by online CPUs (maximum six), `OPAMJOBS`,
+`CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL`, `XGBOOST_BUILD_JOBS`, available Linux memory,
+and cgroup v1/v2 memory limits. Set `XGBOOST_BUILD_JOBS=1` for small or
+emulated builders. Memory budgeting reserves one GiB and allows one GiB per
+compiler process, with a minimum of one job. The opam build exports its selected
+job count through `OPAMJOBS`; for direct Dune builds set `XGBOOST_BUILD_JOBS`
+explicitly to bound the nested CMake build. This heuristic cannot guarantee
+that a machine with insufficient RAM will complete a C++ compilation.
